<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>michi bench — {{ result.target }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf8; --panel: #ffffff; --ink: #1c1b1a; --muted: #6b6764;
    --line: #e6e2dc; --accent: #b23a30; --high: #c0392b; --warn: #b8860b;
    --info: #7a7570; --good: #2e7d32; --bar: #cbd5e1;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #17161a; --panel: #1e1d22; --ink: #ece9e4; --muted: #a09a94;
      --line: #302e35; --accent: #e2645a; --high: #e2645a; --warn: #d4a548;
      --info: #8b8580; --good: #6aab6e; --bar: #3a3942;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 5rem; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.6 ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 940px; margin: 0 auto; }
  header { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .brand { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .brand .kanji { color: var(--accent); margin-right: .4rem; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin-top: .25rem; }
  .stats { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .stat .value { font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .stat .label { color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase;
                 letter-spacing: .06em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em;
       color: var(--muted); margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .card { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px;
          overflow: hidden; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  th { text-align: left; font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em;
       color: var(--muted); padding: .8rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
       font-weight: 600; }
  td { padding: .75rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace; font-size: .9rem; }
  .leader { font-weight: 700; color: var(--good); }
  .tied { color: var(--warn); }
  .failed { color: var(--high); }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .verdict { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line);
             border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px;
             padding: 1rem 1.2rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .sev { font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;
         letter-spacing: .06em; padding: .15rem .5rem; border-radius: 4px; color: #fff; }
  .sev-high { background: var(--high); }
  .sev-warn { background: var(--warn); }
  .sev-info { background: var(--info); }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .86rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
           color: var(--muted); font-size: .82rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <div class="brand"><span class="kanji">道</span>michi bench</div>
  <div class="sub mono">target: {{ result.target }}</div>
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><div class="value">{{ result.results|length }}</div><div class="label">models</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="value">{{ "{:,}".format(result.n_rows) }}</div><div class="label">rows</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="value">{{ result.folds }}</div><div class="label">folds</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="value">{{ result.task }}</div><div class="label">task</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="value">{{ result.primary_metric }}</div><div class="label">ranked by</div></div>
  </div>
</header>

<h2>Results</h2>
<div class="card">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>model</th><th class="num">{{ result.primary_metric }}</th>
          <th class="num">95% interval</th><th>vs leader</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for row in rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="mono {% if row.is_leader %}leader{% endif %}">{{ row.name }}</td>
        <td class="num {% if row.failed %}failed{% endif %}">{{ row.value }}</td>
        <td class="num muted">{{ row.interval }}</td>
        <td class="{% if row.is_leader %}leader{% elif 'tied' in row.verdict %}tied{% elif row.failed %}failed{% else %}muted{% endif %}">{{ row.verdict }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="verdict">
  <strong>Verdict.</strong>
  {% if result.leader %}
    {% if tied %}
      <code>{{ result.leader.name }}</code> scores highest, but
      {% for name in tied %}<code>{{ name }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {{ "is" if tied|length == 1 else "are" }} statistically indistinguishable
      from it at this sample size. Choosing between them on these numbers alone
      is not supported.
    {% else %}
      <code>{{ result.leader.name }}</code> scores highest, and its advantage
      over every other model is statistically significant.
    {% endif %}
  {% else %}
    No model could be trained.
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% if result.checks %}
<h2>Checks</h2>
<div class="card">
  <table>
    <tbody>
    {% for check in result.checks %}
      <tr>
        <td style="width:1%"><span class="sev sev-{{ check.severity.value }}">{{ check.severity.value }}</span></td>
        <td>{{ check.summary }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>How this was measured</h2>
<div class="card">
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="muted" style="width:30%">cross-validation</td><td>{{ result.folds }}-fold{% if result.task == "classification" %}, stratified{% endif %}, shuffled with seed {{ result.seed }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="muted">preparation</td><td>{{ preparation }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="muted">baseline</td><td>a dummy model is always included as the floor</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="muted">significance</td><td>corrected resampled <i>t</i>-test (Nadeau &amp; Bengio, 2003), Holm-adjusted across models</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="muted">intervals</td><td>95% <i>t</i>-interval across folds — optimistic, since folds share training data</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p class="note">
  Intervals describe the spread of fold scores, not true generalisation error.
  The significance test, which corrects for the overlap between training folds,
  is what the verdict relies on.
</p>

<footer>
  michi {{ result.manifests[0].michi_version if result.manifests else "" }} ·
  {{ result.duration_s|round(1) }}s ·
  seed {{ result.seed }}
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
